<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open slightly lower.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open slightly lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open  0.10 cent lower on Friday based on market orders at 1018 EDT, traders  said.</p>
<p>Traders said there were 150 lots of December offered at the opening.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the December contract closed 0.31 cent lower at 75.05  cents a lb, having ranged from 75.30 to 74.65 cents. The rest of the  board ended 0.49 cent to 0.03 cent lower.</p>
<p>((--Doris Frankel, Chicago Commodity Desk, 312-983-7305))</p>
